{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3nfphXgokwMkRnQYnC1","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the spelling in all three files and committed it as one commit, `22d5c23`, so `git revert 22d5c23` undoes it in one go. Each file had one `wholsale` row, and each now reads `wholesale`. I searched the whole repo afterwards and none are left in `data/`. `scripts/check.sh` printed `OK`, and since all three files are 2025, it actually checked them this time.\n\nTwo things to know:\n\n- **The commit message lists three months.** CLAUDE.md says messages start with the data month because the import log is grouped by month, but this one commit covers October, November and December. I started it with `2025-10, 2025-11, 2025-12:`. If the import log tool expects exactly one month at the start, it may misfile this commit or reject it. Keeping it to one commit, as you asked, came first.\n- **`inbox/2025-12.csv` still has the typo.** It's the untracked source copy, so changing it wouldn't show up in the commit anyway. I left it alone, but it would bring the typo back if anyone copies December into `data/` again.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":347,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":426,"cache_read_input_tokens":19718,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":426,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-52>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:44:30.032Z","request_id":"gen-1794703465-NSW8Zj58Plimd8e9s9Od"}
